S 3/0:** wrote B1's expected Error List file; the re-check matched 99/99, with nothing extra and nothing missing.\n- **111-5, BLOCKED:** the prior-art review was right. The B2a rows I chose have no working scripting functions yet: there is no route to shift registers already in the file, and none from a control terminal into a structure tunnel. Cycle 110's brief had already said this tooling comes before B2.\n\n**Review of the cycle:** two faults, both accepted.\n- **Wrong ordering, 13 min, mine:** no new mechanism, since the existing prior-art gate caught it.\n- **Offline-check exemption incomplete, 3 min:** the dry run of a recipe whose prior-art review is still open was exempted in only one of two places; `guard_cycle` still refuses it. That fix is now part of cycle 112's first card.\n\n**Cycle 112's first act** (Pre-decided 225(h) in `docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md`; also in STATUS `## NEXT` and `tools/bench/next.json`):\n1. The hypothesis review blocking every build. `guard_peer` was armed by `diag_c111e_md5.log`, which failed because I put a stale md5 for `stage_d1_l2b1.py` in card 111-5 (`4ef10fc4`; the file is `e13177d9`).\n2. One tooling card for the six missing pieces, (i)–(vi), each checked first on a small scratch VI.\n3. Re-simulate L2-B2a on the saved B1 file, then one launch to `D1_l2_b2a_<ts>.vi` with its expected Error List file.\n\nNo new questions for you from this cycle, and no LabVIEW instance or motor session was left open by my cards.","ttft_ms":1997,"type":"result","duration_ms":6852108,"uuid":"abb506f9-b9e8-4109-9215-82a20d240be6","ttft_stream_ms":1813,"time_to_request_ms":206,"first_content_frame_ms":1813,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
